Package: nanoflow
Title: End-to-End Oxford Nanopore Long-Read Whole-Genome Analysis
    Workflow
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Fiona Katharina", "Meinzer",
           email = "fiona.ewald@stat.uni-muenchen.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Orchestrates an end-to-end Oxford Nanopore long-read
    whole-genome analysis workflow on real sequencing data: optional
    GPU basecalling (Dorado), read QC and trimming (NanoPlot, Porechop,
    Filtlong, MultiQC), alignment (minimap2), optional de novo assembly
    (Flye) with polishing, small-variant calling (Clair3), structural
    variant calling (Sniffles2), haplotype phasing (WhatsHap),
    annotation (SnpEff, AnnotSV), truth-set benchmarking (hap.py,
    Truvari) and an HTML report. The package is an orchestration layer:
    every step wraps an established command-line tool via system2(),
    manages files between steps and returns standard formats (FASTQ,
    BAM, VCF, FASTA). No algorithm is reimplemented. Defaults target
    human GRCh38; reference, models and databases are configurable for
    other diploid organisms. Nanopore reads are the primary input;
    Illumina short reads are an optional per-sample extra used for
    hybrid assembly.
